# Structure

```
src/
  app/          routes, Shell, layout
  catalogue/    contact sheet, plates, detail
  playground/   editor, drafts, export
  harness/      composeSrcDoc, PreviewFrame, ControlStrip
  prompt/       buildPrompt, CopyButton
  specimens/
    types.ts, taxonomy.ts, inspiration.ts, resolvePayload.ts
    index.ts                 # thin barrel (re-exports only)
    registry/
      order.ts               # canonical id order
      shards/<franchise>.ts  # explicit imports per franchise
      assemble.ts            # merges shards → specimens + Maps
    library/<franchise>/<id>/  # demo files (entry, payload, …)
  styles/       tokens.css, base.css
docs/           design-spec.md, ideation/, catalogue/
public/         _redirects, _headers, favicon
scripts/
  spec-new.mjs / spec-check.mjs / spec-ship.mjs
  ephemeral/    # disposable one-shot gens (not supported surface)
```

## Registry

- Specimens live under `library/<franchise>/<id>/` where `<franchise>` matches `inspiredBy.franchise` (or `original`).
- Register by: import in `registry/shards/<franchise>.ts` **and** append `id` to `registry/order.ts`.
- `index.ts` is a **barrel only** — never a mega import list.
- `assemble.ts` enumerates shards with **static imports** (no `import.meta.glob`, no directory scanning).
- Lookups use `specimensById` / `getSpecimen` Maps — do not reintroduce linear `.find` scans.
- Refs (`SPX-001`, …) and display order stay under human control via `order.ts`.
- Each folder splits **light** `entry.ts` (metadata + `loadPayload`) from **`payload.ts`** (`?raw` HTML/CSS/JS + spec + contract). Catalogue ships meta only; previews/detail/copy await `loadPayload` / `resolvePayload`.
